      },
      {
        "typeName": "shape",
        "id": "shape:par_title",
        "type": "text",
        "parentId": "page:page",
        "index": "a00079",
        "x": 826,
        "y": 92,
        "rotation": 0,
        "props": {
          "text": "y = x^2 over x = -4..4",
          "font": "draw",
          "size": "m",
          "color": "blue",
          "textAlign": "start",
          "verticalAlign": "start",
          "w": 350,
          "autoSize": false,
          "scale": 1,
          "url": ""
        },
        "meta": {}
      },
      {
        "typeName": "shape",
        "id": "shape:par_sub",
        "type": "text",
        "parentId": "page:page",
        "index": "a00080",
        "x": 826,
        "y": 376,
        "rotation": 0,
        "props": {
          "text": "r = 0.0 exactly, not approximately. Every +x cancels its -x. Perfectly determined, and invisible to r.",
          "font": "draw",
          "size": "s",
          "color": "grey",
          "textAlign": "start",
          "verticalAlign": "start",
          "w": 350,
          "autoSize": false,
          "scale": 1,
          "url": ""
        },
        "meta": {}
      },
      {
        "typeName": "shape",
        "id": "shape:note1",
        "type": "text",
        "parentId": "page:page",
        "index": "a00081",
        "x": 820,
        "y": 400,
        "rotation": 0,
        "props": {
          "text": "Leverage, same nine x: y = |x| gives r = 2.9e-17. Add one point at (20, 20) and r = 0.90150. That point is not evidence of a trend, it is the trend.",
          "font": "draw",
          "size": "m",
          "color": "black",
          "textAlign": "start",
          "verticalAlign": "start",
          "w": 350,
          "autoSize": false,
          "scale": 1,
          "url": ""
        },
        "meta": {}
      },
      {
        "typeName": "shape",
        "id": "shape:note2",
        "type": "text",
        "parentId": "page:page",
        "index": "a00082",
        "x": 820,
        "y": 470,
        "rotation": 0,
        "props": {
          "text": "Panel IV is not 0.819 \u2014 it is 0.816521, and Anscombe prints 0.817. The real finding is a refusal: delete the single point at x = 19 and the other ten x values are all 8, so Sxx = 0 exactly and r has no denominator. One row was the whole correlation; the other ten could not enter the calculation.",
          "font": "draw",
          "size": "m",
          "color": "black",
          "textAlign": "start",
          "verticalAlign": "start",
          "w": 350,
          "autoSize": false,
          "scale": 1,
          "url": ""
        },
        "meta": {}
      },
      {
        "typeName": "shape",
        "id": "shape:note3",
        "type": "text",
        "parentId": "page:page",
        "index": "a00083",
        "x": 820,
        "y": 540,
        "rotation": 0,
        "props": {
          "text": "And the refusal: if either spread is zero, r is undefined, not small. pearson_r must raise rather than answer 0.0.",
          "font": "draw",
          "size": "m",
          "color": "red",
          "textAlign": "start",
          "verticalAlign": "start",
          "w": 350,
          "autoSize": false,
          "scale": 1,
          "url": ""
        },
        "meta": {}
      },
      {
        "typeName": "shape",
        "id": "shape:credit",
        "type": "text",
        "parentId": "page:page",
        "index": "a00084",
        "x": 40,
        "y": 700,
        "rotation": 0,
        "props": {
          "text": "Generated by make_tldr.py from the published Anscombe (1973) vectors. Every number printed on these panels is asserted against exact rational arithmetic on the same data before the file is written; nothing here is copied from a textbook table. Shared across all four: mean x 9.00, var x 11.00, mean y 7.50, r-squared 0.666. Red line = the least-squares fit of that panel's own points.",
          "font": "draw",
          "size": "s",
          "color": "grey",
          "textAlign": "start",
          "verticalAlign": "start",
          "w": 1130,
          "autoSize": false,
          "scale": 1,
          "url": ""
        },
        "meta": {}
      }
    ]
  },
  "scope": "document"
}
